      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T01:38:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible for `mEnable16k` to change in between when `installUpdate()` is called and when this `onPayloadApplicationComplete()` callback is invoked?\n\nIn between when `mEnable16k` is set and when it is used here is a dialog being shown and an OTA package being applied.\n\nAn alternative to consider would be to pass the intended value of the setting as a parameter so that each invocation chain started by an `onPreferenceChange()` is consistent in whether it is trying to enable 16k or revert back to 4k.\n\nThe same applies for the dialog callbacks. They assume that the value of `mEnable16k` must be the same as the value that was provided to the dialog upon its creation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 279,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 279,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "b22326d333a1dc38fe427ee8988dfeb89e48c451",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a39f0c5_fc2d883e",
        "filename": "src/com/android/settings/development/Enable16kPagesPreferenceController.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 279,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T19:16:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not possible to change from settings. There will be non-cancelable progress dialog and after that device will be restarted. We are using UpdateEngineStable which doesn\u0027t provide cancel API. If anyhow user manages to change it before callback, second update is expected to fail as update engine won\u0027t apply it because of the pending update which will be waiting for reboot.",
      "parentUuid": "196cc5c6_8b163b8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 279,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 279,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "b22326d333a1dc38fe427ee8988dfeb89e48c451",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
